This is the UI of Patient Feedback Analysis

### Functionalities

1️⃣ Core Table / Grid View
    Display all incident records in a Streamlit table.
    Columns: everything from your Excel list.
    Support for sorting, filtering, and searching:
    Search by patient name, incident number, department, category, etc.
    Filter by severity, stage, status, or domain.
    Option to select multiple rows for bulk actions (delete/export).

2️⃣ Add / Insert Record
    Form to create a new incident record.
    Fields map directly from your Excel columns.
    Optional: split into tabs for better UX:
    Tab 1: Basic Info (تاريخ تلقي الملاحظة, الرقم, P. Full Name, etc.)
    Tab 2: Case & Action Details (Immediate Action, الإجراءات المتخذة, etc.)
    Tab 3: Severity & Classification (Severity, Stage, Harm, Status, etc.)
    Button: Save → calls your IncidentAPI.add_incident(record).

3️⃣ Edit / Update Record

    Select a record in the table → open pre-filled form (same as Add form).
    Allow editing all fields.
    Button: Update → calls IncidentAPI.edit_incident(incident_id, record).


4️⃣ Delete Record

    Select a row (or multiple rows) → click Delete.
    Confirmation dialog: “Are you sure?”
    Calls a IncidentAPI.delete_incident(incident_id) function you can implement.

5️⃣ Dashboard

    High-level summary charts and KPIs:
    Number of incidents by Domain (CLINICAL, MANAGEMENT, RELATIONAL).
    Incidents by Severity, Stage, Harm.
    Top 5 Departments with most incidents.
    Pie charts for Category/Sub-Category breakdown.
    Streamlit supports Plotly, Altair, or Matplotlib charts.

6️⃣ Reporting

    Similar to dashboard but more detailed and exportable.
    Example reports:
    All incidents per department for a given month.
    Open incidents vs closed incidents.
    Improvement opportunities (نوع "فرصة التحسين" = yes/no).
    Could be shown as a downloadable Excel/PDF table or chart.

7️⃣ Export

    Export selected or all records as Excel/CSV.
    Could also export filtered tables (e.g., only open incidents).
    Useful for sharing with management or offline analysis.

### Structure
    1. Horizontal Tab that is the menu interesting with a vertical ones that has menu options
    2. On the Intersection (Top Left Corner) Writes Admin and Shows the person who Entered the website
    3. On the Horizontal bar. It is split into (Insert, delete, Export)
    4. The Vertical bar, is split into (Admin - Dashboard , Reporting)
    5. The Page consist of 2 parts
        1. The table part. (Top half of the Page)
            1. Has a search bar for the searchable features (Full Patient Name - Doctor Name - )
            2. Is made of records that has buttons and can be selected at the same time
             (select and export - select and delete - Has an edit button as well)
            3. The records hold all the data of the object. (We could make the record of 2 rows to fit)
            4. Each record is made up of the following things here ( feedback_received_date record_id patient_full_name issuing_department
                  target_department source_1 feedback_type domain category sub_category classification_ar
                  complaint_text immediate_action taken_action severity_level stage harm_level status improvement_opportunity_type  )

        2. The Insert Part. When clicked it should have the following
            1. 2 Main text entry blocks each with dictate option (I have the code of this part)
            2. 2 small NER windows to check the NER of the input data.(Patient Name - Doctor Name)
                (they are empty initially and get filled once we click Extract data button - They are editable)
            3. 8 bars for Classification (They appear once click Extract data button - They are editable as models have
                low precision)
            3. Some Selections I mean select tabs that you can choose from
                (Issuing Department - Targeting Department- Issuing Date - Source1 - New Classification AR)
            4. Extract data button (That runs NER and Classification Models)
            5. Add record button (After manual inspection and editing they can add the record )



